  "review": "Codex Luna Max/ECC read-only reviews of transactional target, shared provider I/O, single-use transfer/denial/cancellation, and three rounds of fork ownership. Actionable findings reproduced and corrected. Final physical connector-spy coverage added and passed; no further production mutation. Lead composition/diff review PASS within stated scope.",
  "scope": [
    "Work reserves2 physical sessions before advisory/transaction and keeps physical scopes separate from transferred lease resources.",
    "Managed target resolution reuses the Work transaction while rechecking pinned engine/configuration/store UUID and receiver/session/window; legacy adapter callback remains compatible.",
    "Work prepare/callback/native worker/receipt/abandonment retain physical loans until exact closure.",
    "Single-use PID/thread/task/lifetime transfer shares sticky denial and joins actual workers across repeated cancellation.",
    "One BaseProvider helper handles70 offloads in9providers; shared readiness4 and create-terminal offloads use the same mechanism. No provider-specific concurrency quota or permission change.",
    "No-start create witness preserves outer cleanup ownership and retires only its allocated checkout; started create drains compensation.",
    "One fork coordinator detaches registered handles before creating child-local close tracking; retains old registry without locks/close/token retirement. Failed detachment prevents unbound connector opening. Inherited scopes/ledgers cannot be rebound; fresh child-owned PostgreSQL works while parent backend stays alive."
